      {
        "name": "why_we_like_it",
        "body": "This Lower Haight omakase destination is making waves. The door is unmarked, and once you find your way inside, you’ll see that there are only six seats at the sushi bar — period. The sushi, though, is fabulous."
      },
      {
        "name": "tagline",
        "body": ""
      },
      {
        "name": "from_the_venue",
        "body": null
      },
      {
        "name": "need_to_know",
        "body": "Cancellation Policy \n\nDue to our limited space and for the sustainability of our small business, we have a strict cancellation policy. Any cancellations, no-shows, or changes to your reservation within 2 days (48 hours; for 1 - 5 people) and 4 days (96 hours; for 6+ people) are subject to a ◉ non-refundable ◉ $150 per guest. Thank you for understanding.\n\nReservations\n\nReservations are available within a 21-day period, released at 11 PM each night. In order to provide the best dining experience, we ask everyone to arrive promptly. For arrivals 15+ minutes late guests may have to join the meal at its current course.\n\nCorkage\n• $50\n• $65 for bottles on our menu\n• Limit one bottle per party (up to 750ml) "
      },
      {
        "name": "about",
        "body": "An intimate 7-seat counter experience (with advance reservations, only). The multi-course omakase menu features fish sourced directly from Tokyo's Toyosu Market as well local, seasonal vegetables.\n\nKEN is the first restaurant and an evolving venture of Chef Ken. He previously developed his passion with Chef Mitsunori Kusakabe over 17 years."
      },
      {
        "name": "pickup_description",
        "body": null
      }
    ]
  }
}

