      "address_1": "430 Columbus Avenue",
      "locality": "San Francisco",
      "region": "CA",
      "postal_code": "94133",
      "country_iso3166": "US"
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "name": "why_we_like_it",
        "body": "This garlic-centric Columbus Avenue icon has been perfuming the air and delighting local palates for three decades. Now serving its well-garlicked salads, sandwiches, pastas, pizzas, and entrées just down the street from its original location, it’s as good as ever. Pro tip: The signature 40-clove garlic roasted chicken is the move."
      },
      {
        "name": "tagline",
        "body": ""
      },
      {
        "name": "from_the_venue",
        "body": null
      },
      {
        "name": "need_to_know",
        "body": "Pets are allowed at outside tables only.  Service animals are always allowed inside and outside.  Reservations are recommended.  Walk-Ins are accepted, however, reservations will be seated first and there could be an extended wait.  Corkage Charge $4.99 per bottle.  Outside bakery items are allowed but can't be held or refrigerated.  Due to fraud, we no longer sell gift cards online or over the phone.  Gift cards can only be purchased in person at the restaurant."
      },
      {
        "name": "about",
        "body": "All you have to do is follow your nose to The Stinking Rose, one of San Francisco’s most unique and entertaining dining experiences.  Located in the heart of North Beach, San Francisco’s renowned Little Italy, the garlic restaurant has become famous for celebrating the euphoria of garlic.  Offering scrumptious, contemporary, California-Italian cuisine prepared and adorned with garlic, there is hearty fare for the truly adventurous, mild for the novice and sans garlic for vampires.\n\n“We season our garlic with food”®\n\nA Fun Dining Restaurant  -  Have a Stinking Good Time!!"
      },
      {
        "name": "pickup_description",
        "body": null
      }
    ]
  }
}

